WEBVTT

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>tsukinuketa aoi sora</b>

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>The blue sky has broken through</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>saa dekakeyou</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>Come, let's go out</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>itsumo no namikimichi jitensha wo koideku</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>Riding my bike through the usual avenue</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>ima sugu ni aitai yo</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>"I want to meet you now."</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.800
<b>omoi ga kaze wo kiri</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.800
<b>That thought is blown away by the wind,</b>

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:44.730
<b>kimi e to hakondeku tegami ni natte</b>

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:44.730
<b>and becomes a letter being carried to you</b>

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:52.320
<b>koko kara hajimaru monogatari fly!</b>

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:52.320
<b>The story that starts from here... Fly!</b>

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>kawariyuku kisetsu ga ashioto wo tatetemo</b>

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>Even if the changing seasons walk on with loud footsteps,</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.460
<b>sou kawaranai suki to iu tsubasa</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.460
<b>the wings of love won't change</b>

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:14.470
<b>dokomade mo tondeke oozora takaku</b>

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:14.470
<b>Fly far away, high into the sky</b>

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:20.720
<b>koi no tenki yohou hare nochi hare ni nare</b>

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:20.720
<b>May the weather forecast of love be sunny and clear forever</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>ashita mo asatte mo</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>Tomorrow and the day after tomorrow</b>

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:36.110
<b>Episode 4    Earth's Crisis</b>

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.610
Thank you for waiting.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.120
The second class of the day is probably starting.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.280
Yurie-sama.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.660
Why is this big lump of iron flying in the air?

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.790
Don't be stupid!

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:52.800
This is the monster bird Tonderera 
that the government secretly keeps.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.300
Of course it can fly.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.170
I see.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.130
Anything that has shape will break.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.970
That means this will someday crash.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.140
Why did I end up doing this?

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.520
<i>Western style sweet jelly paste "Ochikosshi"!</i>

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.020
<i>Very yummy! Now on sale!</i>

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.030
Tama seems to have become 
very smart since returning home.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.320
<i>It's 7:30!</i>

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.030
<i>Yesterday's Diet meeting ended after midnight,</i>

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.740
I'm sure the journey helped Tama mature.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.150
<i>because of the opposition party's stalling tactics.</i>

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:22.200
<i>So, reaching a settlement for the revision plan will now be carried over until tomorrow.</i>

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.200
There is a saying that we must let a pet cat travel.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.120
Oh, what does that mean?

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.000
<i>In response, the ruling government party has criticized the opposition.</i>

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.000
Well, I'm not talking about that kind of thing.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.210
Hey! What's going on with Tama?

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.040
<i>I think their attitude is completely childish.</i>

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.040
<i>The argument goes round and round and gets nowhere.</i>

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.040
Exclusively defensive 
security policy

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.540
<i>We better come to a decision quickly.</i>

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.340
What do you mean?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.010
<i>The Prime Minister has been making compromises with representatives of—</i>

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.340
She's normal.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.840
Normal? That is?!

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.840
<i>other parties, and is trying to resolve the situation smoothly.</i>

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.970
Shou-chan, you should eat breakfast quietly.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.590
<i>But his plan seems to have backfired on him.</i>

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.970
<i>The Cabinet's approval rate is now less than 30%.</i>

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.770
Akane-san is right.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:48.430
You won't grow well if you  are being obnoxious first thing in the morning.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:49.560
<i>Yurie, I shouldn't have done that sort of thing?</i>

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.350
Nobody pays attention to what I say!

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.690
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.060
<i>My mom and dad are both easygoing.</i>

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.650
<i>We can persuade Shou-chan too somehow.</i>

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.900
<i>I can't tell them that we have a poverty god in the house.</i>

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.400
<i>Not only the opposition party, but some of the younger members—</i>

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.900
<i>Of the government party are complaining about—</i>

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.820
<i>So, please keep quiet for a while.</i>

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.820
<i>the Prime Minister's stubborn attitude.</i>

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.330
<i>The revised plan is supposed to be approved today at the Diet.</i>

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.240
Yuri-chan.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.830
You shouldn't eat and read at the same time.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.540
<i>On the other hand, the government party might hold—</i>

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:08.540
It's bad manners.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.000
But, I have a test today.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.000
<i>A big meeting shortly to reconsider the policy.</i>

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.250
<i>However, they haven't had as much support as they'd hoped for—</i>

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.750
What's the matter?

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.380
<i>from the people, so they seem to have chosen other tactics.</i>

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.210
Oh, nothing.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.130
Where are you going?

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.140
Oh, she really has bad manners.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:30.180
What's this?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.270
Thank you for waiting.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.110
We were sent by the God Association.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.070
We are the collection and delivery team, "Happiness"!

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.070
The one that Yashima-sama was telling me about.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.410
We can take care of managing and 
selecting the requests that come to you.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.580
In the meantime, your divine 
power will increase rapidly.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.630
Thank you so much.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.920
We'll be rushing in headlong to work for you, Yurie-sama!

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.630
Well, as many wishes that we deliver to you—

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.010
there are as many wishes that are being disregarded.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.770
We brought a very special wish 
as our greeting gift for you.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.920
Is this the wish?

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.020
From who?

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.230
Yurie-sama.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.110
Well, it seems like there's something serious going on.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.700
<i>I will repeat this again.</i>

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.620
<i>Today, before dawn, the Japanese government has announced that—</i>

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.620
Is this a new drama?

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.620
<i>intelligent life from Mars has visited our country.</i>

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.080
I think so.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:36.040
A long time ago, an actor named Orson 
Wells said similar things on the radio.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.460
<i>The purpose of the visit has not been determined yet.</i>

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:38.040
<i>We'll continue to report on this as soon as we have new information.</i>

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:36.080
We're in trouble. Please help us.
Prime Minister

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:36.130
We're in trouble. Please help us.
Prime Minister

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:36.170
We're in trouble. Please help us.
Prime Minister

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:36.210
We're in trouble. Please help us.
Prime Minister

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:36.250
We're in trouble. Please help us.
Prime Minister

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:36.670
We're in trouble. Please help us.
Prime Minister

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.420
I wonder if we have class today.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.000
We're in trouble. Please help us.
Prime Minister

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.130
She's late—

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.350
Mitsue-chan!

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.890
I'm going to miss school today for official duty!

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.440
Sorry!

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.230
I'm going to Tokyo!

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.400
I'll bring back a souvenir for you!

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.280
I wonder if I can go home today.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.330
Hey, you guys, what are your names?

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.910
Team Happiness!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.460
Oh, no.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.970
Does each one of you have a name?

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.130
No, we don't.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.550
Can you give us names, if you don't mind?

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.130
Me?

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.010
Yes.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.720
Well, all right.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.810
I'm good at giving people names anyway.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.810
<i>We will be arriving soon at Haneda airport.</i>

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.230
<i>Please fasten your seatbelts.</i>

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.340
It's really a UFO.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.600
Welcome to the Prime Minister's official residence.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.530
Are you nervous?

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.740
I'm sorry.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:30.160
This is my first time meeting a Prime Minister.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.870
This is my first time meeting a god, too.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.000
Are you really a god?

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.910
Yes, though I just became one.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.120
I see.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.540
How did you become a god?

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.170
I don't really know how.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.720
Is she really a god?

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.100
The Meteorological Agency says yes.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.390
She and my granddaughter aren't much different.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.100
Since we can't communicate with 
that thing through our language,

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.940
I want you to find out why it came here.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:06.780
That thing?

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.190
Are you all right?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.570
But I don't know how to speak Martian language.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.910
Just use your god power to do that.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.750
The divine power, you know?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:26.130
Anyhow, we captured it and put it 
into a nuclear fallout shelter for now.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.840
It's really a Martian.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.970
I wonder why it came here.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:43.310
But, I wonder if this is the right thing to do.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:47.150
We don't even know its purpose, 
but we're detaining it like this—

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.990
So, can you ask it why it's here?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.910
I'm not quite ready for this yet.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.120
Diplomacy is simply guts!

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.580
Wait! Time out!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:58.910
Let me start all over again!

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.050
Hello—

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.100
I have no clue.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:19.310
Yurie-sama! Fight!

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.520
A Martian is also a human!

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.660
Sincerity is the important thing.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.560
Well, actually Martians are not human—

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:26.560
Stupid!

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.940
Being alone in a foreign country far away.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.700
How would you feel if it happened to you?

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.590
I see.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:35.570
That's right.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:36.960
Thank you.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:37.870
I'll try.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.080
All right!

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.580
Ni hao!

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.350
I'm Yurie.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:50.130
Don't be scared.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.890
Not scared, right?

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.440
Not scared. Not scared.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:10.700
<i>Please.</i>

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.110
<i>Let me out of here.</i>

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.400
Was that you?

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.240
<i>Give me a phone.</i>

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.740
Phone?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.830
<i>The government called on the middle school girl god,</i>

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.880
<i>Hitotsubashi Yurie to act as a diplomat to the Martian.</i>

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.090
<i>Yurie-sama is now talking to the Martian—</i>

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.090
<i>at the Prime Minister's official residence.</i>

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.720
Official duty means that?

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:36.630
Right.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.970
Can you hear me?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.560
Great.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.440
It's just like an earthling's language.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:49.520
Good.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.820
I thought I wouldn't be able to go back to Mars.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.570
Oh, you are a girl just like I thought.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:59.240
I'm sorry that we confined you like this.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.950
I guess all you guys here are nice people.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.660
You guys?

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.290
Can you see us?

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.330
Yes.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.130
People from the government can't see you all.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:17.130
Only pure minded people can see us.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.680
Don't just make things up!

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.350
So, why did you come to Earth?

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.520
I brought back a lost child.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:34.480
A kid who strayed into our land stopped moving.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.700
So, we thought he got bored of playing with us.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:40.910
We all thought that we better send him back to Earth.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.700
So, I brought him back here.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:48.660
Oh, thank you very much for taking 
him back to such a far away planet.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.330
He looks like this.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.090
This is from America.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.920
It says NASA here.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.800
He's not from this country?

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.370
Ours is called NASDA.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.550
It's slightly different.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:04.260
This is the first time I came to Earth.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.600
Well, it's just an octopus, but their technology is incredible.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.430
That happens a lot. Just like me.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.190
I was thinking that Koshien was in Osaka until last year.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:08.640
I won't let it go back.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.200
I'll turn it over to you with the UFO.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:13.310
When I found out it was actually in Hyogo.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:13.310
I'm always on America's side.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.900
So, that's what happened.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:19.320
So, please give her the map 
to get to NASA and release her.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:20.540
I understand.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:21.950
Thank you for your hard work.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.240
The request has been accomplished.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:26.990
A happy ending!

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:28.910
Really?

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:31.580
In appreciation, please take this money.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:34.000
Oh, no! I can't take it.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.890
It's not a bribe.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:38.260
Well, if you insist, then—

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.880
Can you donate it to the Raifuku Shrine?

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.680
Well then, I won't force you to take it.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:47.390
Would you wait in the other room 
until we prepare the helicopter for you?

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.680
Excuse me—

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.850
there is one place I want to go.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.810
The case is settled now.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:59.440
Yes, I think sincerity is very important.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.780
Just like Chou-chan said.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:03.410
Note: chouchou = butterfly

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:03.410
Chou-chan?

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:04.950
That's your name.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.080
Your advice was very useful.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.580
You don't like this name?

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:12.410
Well—

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.420
It is just because your daily behavior is good.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:19.170
Yurie-sama, hooray!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.420
All right.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.510
What am I going to buy as a souvenir?

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:28.010
Sign: Leader of the World - Prime Minister

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.470
I guess I'll pass on this.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:31.270
I wonder if this thing is really settled.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:33.730
I don't trust politicians.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.400
Don't worry.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:38.480
I don't think the Prime Minister would lie.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.230
Look!

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:39.940
What is that?

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.150
The UFO will fall down.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.270
The chopper is unstable.

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:55.420
We'll land at once.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.420
Roger! I'll send some help over there.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:02.090
Stop right there.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.130
Civilians shouldn't get any closer to here.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:16.770
I'm an insider.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.190
I'm terribly sorry.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.110
Let go of me!

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:26.110
I can fly over there with my own ship.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.910
It's not your ship anymore.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.580
It's already the property of the United States.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.790
And, just to let you know, so are you.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.080
You lied to me.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:38.580
You and your ship will help to improve 
our country's technology tremendously.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.590
Prime Minister!

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.380
What's going on?

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:45.090
I told you to release the Martian.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.470
This is not my doing.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:49.680
The director of the Minister's Secretariat is doing this.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:54.520
I guess there must be some sort of miscommunication.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.270
I'll make a note of it.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.270
Why are you playing dumb like that?!

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.230
Take her away.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.650
What are you doing?!

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:00.940
Yurie-chan!

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.150
Let me go!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:04.190
Put me down! Put me down!

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.320
Yurie, give me the radio transmitter!

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.390
What— is this?

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:33.510
Don't take it off.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.060
You won't get sleepy if you keep it on.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:41.900
Let's go.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.400
Headquarters respond!

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.610
We are awaiting your instructions.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.910
I guess the battery is out.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:55.450
Let's go!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.500
<i>An incident has happened at the Diet Building!</i>

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:05.050
<i>Both the Martian and god have escaped.</i>

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.590
<i>They still seem to be hiding inside the Diet Building.</i>

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.800
<i>Everyone rush to the scene!</i>

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.720
<i>We haven't confirmed if they are armed or not.</i>

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.390
<i>Do not lower your guard!</i>

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:22.100
<i>The Martian and the underage god "A" are—</i>

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.400
<i>currently hiding inside the Diet building.</i>

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:27.530
<i>This unusual activity inside the Diet building is—</i>

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.530
What is she doing?

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.700
I hope this doesn't become a serious incident.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.700
<i>Creating havoc in the area.</i>

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:32.070
It's already become very serious!

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:36.240
Emergency 
Headquarters

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.240
The Metropolitan Police Department should move in now!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.130
No.

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:41.210
Since this is an invasion by Martians, 
the Defense Agency should move in!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.670
Let's leave this up to the U.S. Military.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.000
The U.S.-Japan Security Treaty 
exists for this kind of incident.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.750
This is a diplomatic problem, so the Ministry 
of Foreign Affairs should take care of it.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:48.880
Enough of this already!

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.680
This is an emergency situation.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.930
I'll take charge of this.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:59.560
The secret service, SWAT and self defense 
forces should all follow my orders!

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.940
First of all, we must recall the 
radio transmitters from every unit!

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.400
It's turned into a big uproar.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.240
I'm sorry.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.400
This is all because of me.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:13.110
No, I think that the Prime Minister is wrong.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.530
I'm sorry.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:18.620
I never thought that the leader of 
our country was such a bad person.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.500
But you guys were doing this to help me.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.420
So, don't feel bad.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.040
Oh, it just came to me now.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:29.550
Let's make your name Ino-kun.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:29.550
Note: inoshishi = boar

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.470
Yes!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:37.860
Yes, if you can imagine another 
person's feelings it's easy to figure out.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:40.560
Anyone wants to go back home.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.190
People have families who are waiting for them.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:45.440
Right?

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:52.900
Who is that?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.660
Someone whom I like.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:00.370
He's my classmate in Mars Middle School.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.040
But I don't know how he feels about me.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.920
Are you also a middle school student?

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.670
And you also have someone whom you like.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:09.960
What do you mean "also"?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.580
Nothing, just forget it.

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:19.220
Now, I really want to send you back home.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.020
I think Martians belong on Mars!

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.770
My mom always says after she 
comes back from her trip—

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.350
"Oh, there's no place like home."

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.400
But how should we handle this?

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.690
We need to reach the ship,

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.410
but there are many government 
agents waiting to capture us.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:39.320
I got it!

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.660
Hey, can you look for a pen and paper for me?

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:45.540
I have it.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.790
Please use them.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.330
Thank you.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.380
But, I only have three pieces of paper.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:52.500
It's so small.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.010
Three pieces—

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.550
I hope this works out well.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:56.970
What are you trying to do?

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.930
Prepare the breakout operation.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.430
I think you better open your eyes when you write.

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.680
My eyes are open!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:06.450
You don't have anybody who 
can teach you how to write?

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:07.190
I don't—

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:10.020
well, that may not be true— but—

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:16.150
You always say weird things!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.820
As punishment, your name is Shika-kun!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.820
Note: shika = deer

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.280
I happily accept it!

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.290
Even if it is a punishment?

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.580
Now everyone has names.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:28.750
Hooray!

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.310
Give yourselves up!

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:36.840
We know you guys are in there!

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:38.840
Just surrender quietly!

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.010
There are so many of them.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:43.260
They're coming over here!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.770
"Technique", how can I write that character?

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:47.480
Like this and this and this!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:49.770
Here they come!

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:51.440
Finished!

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:03.030
Great work, Yurie-sama!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:05.540
I did it.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.960
Sign: Slowness Technique

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.540
What am I going to do next?

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:10.830
Report what's going on!

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:13.380
Since we can't use the radio 
transmitters, please wait a moment.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.670
Target sighted.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.050
Secure them!

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.860
<i>The second and third platoons should act as support teams.</i>

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:31.100
<i>First platoon shouldn't leave their position!</i>

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.660
Watch out, it's gas!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:46.910
Sign: Fake product

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:46.620
Everyone put on their masks!

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.040
Circumstances may justify a lie!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.800
Going in a straight line is not the only way.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:53.420
I wonder if Yurie-sama will be all right.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:02.430
Are we going to be all right?

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:05.510
I have one more piece of 
paper that Ino-chan gave me.

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:06.810
So, we can make it.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:07.760
Don't move!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.060
Put your hands up!

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:20.940
Yurie-chan!

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:23.280
What am I going to do?

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.910
Exclusively defensive security policy!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.210
The defensive power of our country is—

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.210
well—

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:39.420
only to be used if another 
country launches a military attack—

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.380
it should only use— no—

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.470
take the minimum action necessary.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:49.930
You shouldn't take any 
action except in those cases—

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:54.480
In other words, you have no right to attack us.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.480
If you'll excuse us.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.320
Here we go.

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:10.330
Oh, no!

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:12.620
Don't look at us, you pervert!

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.460
This is it!

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:24.590
I'll turn that octopus over to 
the United States, no matter what.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:25.470
Why?

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:29.680
It's only natural the little 
Martian should go back to Mars.

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.560
This is what diplomacy is all about.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:39.150
We don't have any interest in a planet that
 would take millions of dollars just to visit.

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:41.190
Now! Give that octopus to me!

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:42.860
For Japan!

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:44.650
For the United States!

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:45.150
Let me go!

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.160
For the good of our two countries' relationship!

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:04.670
Are you all right?

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:17.890
Thank you very much for everything.

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:18.810
It was nothing.

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:22.690
Please don't hate the earthlings because of this.

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:24.780
There aren't only bad people on earth.

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:27.900
There are also great people like Yurie-sama.

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:32.660
Yes, and good people like you guys, too.

00:22:35.660 --> 00:22:37.960
Please come and visit Mars sometime.

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:40.920
I'll try hard to do that.

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:44.380
I want to meet your friends too.

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:47.800
Let's do our best.

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:49.880
Yes, do our best.

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:55.390
Oh, this?

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:56.770
You can keep it.

00:22:57.140 --> 00:22:57.890
Really?

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:00.490
Thank you.

00:23:00.490 --> 00:23:02.270
Then I'll give you something, too.

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:08.320
Here.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:09.570
Thank you.

00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:12.990
Martian-chan

00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:12.990
Martian-kun

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:12.990
What does it say?

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:14.740
You'll know when you get back.

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:17.250
Take care.

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:19.790
Yes.

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.180
See you soon!

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:41.140
Now it's finally settled.

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:42.780
I hope so.

00:23:42.780 --> 00:23:43.520
Yes.

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:45.270
Yes.

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:51.700
I wonder if they will give me a ride back home?

00:23:56.050 --> 00:23:58.720
<i>The United Nations announced that the Viking spacecraft left in front of—</i>

00:23:58.720 --> 00:24:01.290
<i>the White House yesterday was deposited by the visiting Martian.</i>

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:04.250
You must have had a hard time.

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.500
<i>And, a message from the Martians was sent to the United Nations—</i>

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:05.500
That's right.

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:07.500
I have a souvenir for you.

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:09.510
<i>Saying that they have great appreciation for Yurie-sama's diplomacy.</i>

00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:13.050
<i>Our Prime Minister made this comment—</i>

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:11.880
Thanks.

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:17.560
<i>Well, our government is considering giving—</i>

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:17.140
Yurie-sama. Good morning.

00:24:17.560 --> 00:24:19.930
<i>the National Honor Award to Yurie-sama.</i>

00:24:17.970 --> 00:24:19.390
We brought you a new request!

00:24:27.650 --> 00:24:29.280
<i>We have a breaking news flash.</i>

00:24:29.280 --> 00:24:31.360
<i>The government has announced that they made contact with—</i>

00:24:31.360 --> 00:24:32.530
<i>people living at the bottom of the sea and—</i>

00:24:32.530 --> 00:24:33.860
<i>deep beneath the surface of the Earth.</i>

00:24:33.860 --> 00:24:35.450
<i>To begin communications with both groups—</i>

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:39.740
Mitsue-chan, I guess I have 
to miss class again today.

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:37.950
<i>they are planning to call on the god Yurie-sama—</i>

00:24:37.950 --> 00:24:39.740
<i>just like they did before.</i>

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:49.510
<b>mada mada zenzen owannai last ichijikan no jugyou desu</b>

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:49.510
<b>The last class of the day never seems to end</b>

00:24:49.510 --> 00:24:54.360
<b>tokei wo chira chira mitemo ichi byou ga nagai ne</b>

00:24:49.510 --> 00:24:54.360
<b>Even if I keep glancing at my watch, a second seems an eternity</b>

00:24:55.420 --> 00:25:01.450
<b>mabushii koutei mieru kimi no hashiru sugata oikake</b>

00:24:55.420 --> 00:25:01.450
<b>In the radiant schoolyard, trailing your running visage,</b>

00:25:01.450 --> 00:25:06.610
<b>houkago love-love date mousou shite bosou chuu</b>

00:25:01.450 --> 00:25:06.610
<b>my imagination is running wild about our date after class</b>

00:25:07.490 --> 00:25:10.510
<b>chime no kane koi no signal</b>

00:25:07.490 --> 00:25:10.510
<b>The school chimes ring and it's a signal of love!</b>

00:25:10.510 --> 00:25:13.500
<b>rouka no tobidashi ni wa chuui</b>

00:25:10.510 --> 00:25:13.500
<b>Be careful if you rush out into the hallway!</b>

00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:16.490
<b>kimi no moto e ichiban saki ni</b>

00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:16.490
<b>I dash to see you, first thing!</b>

00:25:16.490 --> 00:25:19.090
<b>issho ni kaerou</b>

00:25:16.490 --> 00:25:19.090
<b>Let's go home together!</b>

00:25:20.070 --> 00:25:26.730
<b>soda aji no ice candy gira gira na ohisama no shita hanbunko</b>

00:25:20.070 --> 00:25:26.730
<b>Sharing a soda-flavored popsicle under the glaring sun</b>

00:25:26.730 --> 00:25:32.770
<b>torokesou na atashi no seishun desu doki doki shichau</b>

00:25:26.730 --> 00:25:32.770
<b>My youth seems to melt with it, it makes my heart beat faster</b>

00:25:32.770 --> 00:25:38.210
<b>kono nanigenai toki wo ima mune ni shimatte</b>

00:25:32.770 --> 00:25:38.210
<b>I'm shutting our casual time in my heart</b>

00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:45.670
<b>asu wa mata kyou yori mo kimi wo suki ni naru no desu</b>

00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:45.670
<b>Tomorrow I will love you even more than today</b>

00:25:49.870 --> 00:26:04.870
<b>Preview</b>

00:25:51.190 --> 00:25:54.530
A god can also catch a cold and have a fever.

00:25:54.900 --> 00:25:56.660
And want to eat pudding.

00:25:57.950 --> 00:26:00.370
Next episode is "I don't like being alone".

00:25:59.780 --> 00:26:04.870
<b>I don't like being alone</b>

00:26:00.370 --> 00:26:02.870
From inside the futon, I'll give you chu!
